$ nexoctl quota info mem/photos
`mem/photos` has no quota.

$ nexoctl quota set mem/photos --size 1.5GiB
Set a hard quota of 1.5GiB on `mem/photos`.

$ nexoctl quota info mem/photos
`mem/photos` has a hard quota of 1.5GiB.

$ nexoctl quota info --json mem/photos
{"status":"success","target":"mem/photos","bucket":"photos","type":"hard","size":1610612736}

$ nexoctl quota set mem/photos
! nexoctl: error: --size is required (use "quota clear" to remove the quota)
! Run 'nexoctl quota set --help' for usage.
[exit 2]

$ nexoctl quota set mem/photos --size 0
! nexoctl: error: --size must be positive (use "quota clear" to remove the quota)
! Run 'nexoctl quota set --help' for usage.
[exit 2]

$ nexoctl quota set mem/photos/key --size 1GiB
! nexoctl: error: mem/photos/key: quota applies to ALIAS/BUCKET
! Run 'nexoctl quota set --help' for usage.
[exit 2]

$ nexoctl quota set bob/photos --size 1GiB
! nexoctl: error: bob/photos: admin:SetBucketQuota: no policy allows admin:SetBucketQuota (access_denied)
[exit 4]

$ nexoctl quota clear mem/photos
Removed the quota of `mem/photos`.

$ nexoctl quota info mem/photos
`mem/photos` has no quota.

$ nexoctl encrypt info mem/photos
`mem/photos`: no default encryption.

$ nexoctl encrypt set sse-s3 mem/photos
Default encryption of `mem/photos`: SSE-S3 (AES256).

$ nexoctl encrypt info mem/photos
`mem/photos`: SSE-S3 (AES256).

$ nexoctl encrypt set sse-kms mem/photos --kms-key-id nexo-key
Default encryption of `mem/photos`: SSE-KMS with key nexo-key.

$ nexoctl encrypt info --json mem/photos
{"status":"success","target":"mem/photos","bucket":"photos","algorithm":"aws:kms","kmsKeyId":"nexo-key"}

$ nexoctl encrypt set sse-s3 mem/photos --kms-key-id k
! nexoctl: error: --kms-key-id needs sse-kms
! Run 'nexoctl encrypt set --help' for usage.
[exit 2]

$ nexoctl encrypt set rot13 mem/photos
! nexoctl: error: unknown encryption "rot13" (sse-s3 or sse-kms)
! Run 'nexoctl encrypt set --help' for usage.
[exit 2]

$ nexoctl encrypt clear mem/photos
Removed the default encryption of `mem/photos`.

$ nexoctl encrypt info mem/photos
`mem/photos`: no default encryption.

